WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
These readings compare two battles on California streets.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.749
Ridesharing won legal status in about a year.

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:10.864
Self driving cars have had a harder road.

00:00:10.864 --> 00:00:13.600
Why did one story go so much better?

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.307
Researchers found three reasons San Francisco welcomed ridesharing.

00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:20.695
Politicians backed local industry.

00:00:20.695 --> 00:00:23.084
The taxi system was dysfunctional.

00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:27.440
And the rules had gray areas, so the fight moved to the state.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.317
The founder of Sidecar tells the inside story.

00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:35.784
His team used donations to work in a legal gray area.

00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:39.577
Sidecar launched in early 2012 and was a hit.

00:00:39.577 --> 00:00:41.600
Richer rivals still won.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.695
In 2018 an Uber test car killed a pedestrian in Tempe.

00:00:45.695 --> 00:00:48.880
Investigators found a weak safety culture.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:55.098
Uber cut from two safety drivers to one, and Arizona collected no safety data from

00:00:55.098 --> 00:00:56.160
the companies.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.654
Cruise was the bold challenger.

00:00:58.654 --> 00:01:02.919
In October 2023 one of its cars dragged a pedestrian.

00:01:02.919 --> 00:01:09.275
ABC7 reports that Cruise first gave regulators an edited video that omitted the

00:01:09.275 --> 00:01:10.000
dragging.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.938
The fallout was swift.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.373
Cruise paused operations in every city.

00:01:15.373 --> 00:01:21.452
By early 2024 it was off public roads, and GM absorbed what remained.

00:01:21.452 --> 00:01:24.800
Trust, once lost, was hard to rebuild.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.130
Timothy Lee wrote as the Cruise CEO quit.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:34.629
Uber's self driving program, he noted, never regained momentum and was sold off.

00:01:34.629 --> 00:01:40.560
Waymo, backed by deep pockets, now stood alone, two to three years ahead.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.193
Takeaway: rules, money, and trust all mattered.

00:01:44.193 --> 00:01:48.290
Ridesharing had friendly regulators and eager riders.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:52.310
Self driving companies faced deaths and concealment.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.640
Candor with regulators may matter as much as technology.
